 "notes": [
  "Sources: FY figures from each year's URD (2022 URD pp.398-401 statements; 2023 URD pp.416-419; 2024 URD pp.370-373; 2025 URD pp.364-367), current-year column as originally reported. Sector/geo constant-currency growth and cur_total taken from the FY press releases (one decimal, e.g. 23.4%); URD tables print the same rounded to whole % (2025 URD prints totals 5.5%/8.9%). Quarterly revenue (Q1-Q4) from the 'Quarterly revenue' table of each FY press release.",
  "'-' (nil) printed in statements recorded as 0 (nonrec, goodwill 2022, disposal lines, borrowing subscriptions); '(0)' recorded as 0.",
  "memo.da_fixed / da_rou = totals incl. amounts in cost of sales as stated under the 'Other income and expenses' note (2022: 341/266; 2023: 378/288; 2024: 427/333; 2025: 448/351). The OI&E line itself shows only part: D&A of fixed assets 288/319/363/381 and ROU amortisation 263/285/330/348 for 2022-2025. impairment = 'Impairment losses' line of that note (123/106/83/127). Values recorded as positive.",
  "2022 cash-flow statement shows D&A of fixed assets (341), depreciation of ROU (266) and impairment (123) as three separate lines (in cf_other); no combined line printed, so cf.da and memo.da_cf are null for 2022. The 2023 URD comparative shows the combined line as 730 for 2022.",
  "2022 URD note 11.1 states share capital of 105,569,412 shares 'of which 108,472 treasury shares' — inconsistent with §7.2.2.4 (1,033,625 treasury shares at 31/12/2022, 1.0% of capital) and with equity treasury shares of €674m; treasury_shares uses 1,033,625 (2022 URD p.~489). Likely a typo in note 11.1.",
  "Treasury shares at year-end: 2023 839,115 (2023 URD note 11.1/§7.2.2.4); 2024 731,644 (2024 URD note 13.1); 2025 733,097 (2025 URD note 12.1).",
  "Adjusted free cash flow 2022: URD prints 3,404 (note 2.4); the FY2022 and FY2023 press releases print 3,405. URD figure used.",
  "Headcount definition change: 2022 (19,686) and 2023 (22,037) per original URDs = permanent + fixed-term contracts > 9 months. From 2024 URD, CSRD definition (all permanent + fixed-term, no seniority condition): 2024 25,185, 2025 26,494; restated pro forma 2023 22,879 and 2022 20,296.",
  "Dividends: FY2022 ordinary €13.00 (interim €3.50 paid 22/02/2023). FY2023 ordinary €15.00 + exceptional €10.00 (proposed to AGM 30/04/2024, paid May 2024). FY2024 ordinary €16.00 + exceptional €10.00 (AGM 30/04/2025, paid May 2025). FY2025 ordinary €18.00 (interim €5.00 paid 18/02/2026), no exceptional. dps_exceptional is recorded in respect of the fiscal year it was proposed with.",
  "2025 French exceptional contribution on large companies' profits: €331m tax expense (2025 URD note 7.2 'exceptional tax contribution (331)', p.381) => memo.excep_tax=331. ETR 33.4% reported, 28.5% excluding the contribution. Net income attributable excluding the contribution printed only as '€4.86 billion, up by 5.5%' (FY2025 PR p.3; 2025 URD §1.8.1) => ni_excl_excep=4860 (rounded as printed in € billions). Net margin 30.3% excluding contribution. Operating cash flows restated for the contribution 'amounted to €5.9 billion, up 10%'.",
  "No other non-recurring income/expenses in 2022-2025 (line printed '-').",
  "Notable items in OI&E: 2022 includes €61m new five-year commitment to the Fondation d'entreprise Hermès (2023-2027); free share plan expenses 65/151/180/199 (2022-2025).",
  "Balance-sheet layout change in 2024 URD: 'Investment property' and 'Loans and deposits' no longer shown separately (2023 comparative restated: PPE 2,347 = 2,340 + investment property 7; other non-current assets 107 = 37 + loans and deposits 70). For 2022/2023 investment property is in bs_other and loans_deposits separate; for 2024/2025 loans_deposits=null (included in other_nca).",
  "2022 URD: IFRIC decision on SaaS configuration costs applied from 1 Jan 2022: intangible assets decreased by €49m, €36m net of deferred tax posted through equity (not restated). Russia stores closed from March 2022, assets written down for a non-significant amount.",
  "2023: acquisitions of consolidated shares €288m in the cash flow; goodwill rose from 0 to 72 and investments in associates from 54 to 200. 2024: Hermès became majority shareholder (Jan 2024) of UAE retail activities with its Middle East partner (not significant per PR); geographic 'Other' renamed 'Other (Middle East)' and grew +110% (scope effect).",
  "Segment 'Unallocated' recurring operating income swings: 2022 -6, 2023 +6, 2024 +331, 2025 +289 (includes free share plan expenses, unallocated central costs and internal billings).",
  "2022 balance sheet: printed sum of non-current asset lines (5,632 incl. investment property 8) differs from printed total 5,630 by 2 due to rounding; totals kept as printed.",
  "2024 cash flow statement (2024 URD p.373) prints financing 'Other' as (2), but the lines then sum to -3,050 vs printed total (3,046); the 2025 URD comparative prints 2024 'Other' as +2, which reconciles. Value kept as originally printed (-2); likely a sign typo in the 2024 URD.",
  "Rounding differences (as printed, totals kept): 2022 non-current assets lines sum 5,632 vs 5,630; 2023 equity attributable lines 15,203 vs 15,201; 2023 operating cash flow lines sum 5,126 vs 5,123 (same in 2024 URD comparative); 2024 non-current liabilities 2,122 vs 2,120; 2025 current assets 15,909 vs 15,911; 2025 equity attributable 18,842 vs 18,840; 2023 quarterly revenue sums to 13,426 vs 13,427. All other identities hold within ±1.",
  "IFRS 16 applies throughout (lease liabilities/ROU on balance sheet; lease repayments in financing, deducted in adjusted FCF)."
 ]
